+## Latest clean result with repaired history and equal-size identity mismatch
+
+Fixture: `metrics identities: latest completions, historical fixes, unique landings and concrete set differences`.
+The input repeats a landing and durable fix record, then appends a clean completion,
+plus ordinary execution metadata and a baseAbsorbed record. Unsupported-version and
+oversized Recovery inputs appearing only at Finish retain their explicit gaps.
+
+```text
+Metrics: merges 1 · merge-failed 0 · rebase-conflicts 0 · seam-reviews 0 (fixed 0) · check-fails 0 (fixed 0)
+Metrics: completions — review clean 1 · after fix pass 0 · parked 0 · re-entry closes 0 · dispatched early 0 · cancelled 0
+Metrics: fix-pass — entered 0 · FIXED 0 · BLOCKED 0 (legacy event lines); durable attempts 1 · historical FIXED 1; repaired findings unavailable (use scope-dispositions --project)
+Metrics: ledger-check ok · append-failed 0 · append-retried 0 · scope: observed ledger; completed after available tracker reconciliation · git-only [bd-999] · ledger-only-git [bd-101] · gaps: Finish recovery: unsupported recovery version; Recovery gap: 99 progress.md; ledger/Git identities differ
+```
+
+Supported reading: one observed task landing and one latest clean completion; one
+retained historical FIXED record. The Git observation identifies bd-999 while ledger
+and completed identify bd-101. Those concrete differences remain unresolved; no cause
+is established. A task FIXED record supplies no repaired-finding count.
